{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Phase 2 complete, pushed as Gerrit 1175 (Change-Id I4e73f709). RED->GREEN with mutation check. RED oracle: tests/unit/test_plan_relation_snapshot.py::test_signer_and_gate_material_agree_across_archive - baseline (all live) signer==gate, then archiving a child made signer keep it (9f28...) while gate dropped it (448e...) -> RED for the exact mechanism. GREEN via one shared predicate counts_as_plan_material_child (live only: excludes archived+deleted) plus a live_material_children gate helper that enumerates WIDE (include_archived=True) and narrows through it, so signer and gate cannot drift (AC1). Second test test_archived_child_excluded_from_child_ids_and_pins pins AC5 (archived child drops from child_ids AND plan-material-pins). Mutation note: reverting ONLY the shared helper makes both sides wrong SYMMETRICALLY (agreement test still passes), but the exclusion test catches it - the two tests are complementary, covering both divergence and symmetric-inclusion regressions. Actual files changed: relation_snapshot.py, attest.py, test_plan_relation_snapshot.py (NOT generation.py - it derives from snapshot.child_ids, fixed at source; NOT test_plan_material_pins.py - existing pin coverage stayed green). attest.py held at exactly 800 LOC (net-zero gate change via the shared helper + existing line-40 import). Gates: 29 unit + 94 plan-review lifecycle gate tests, lint, typecheck all green."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785616223574599001,"uuid":"a2a5f299-f4b5-4c0a-a7b6-9ef76a901e95"}